(Indigenous Tangkhul Text / Chants / Sayings:) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  "Thisham phanitli mangla khangaso, Kasa Akhavali chatkavai.") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  "Mairong kakhonli lambali horho, avava apuipui wui shongshen.") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  "Thisham laa sada wuklungli kachap, mangla katharana kachingli kara.") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 10 Tf
(English Translation & Meaning:) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  "At Thisham feast, we commune with the souls of the departed as they) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  journey to Kasa Akhava.") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  "Pine torches illuminate the mountain pathways, guiding the footsteps of) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  our ancestral beloved.") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  "Singing solemn laments with contrite hearts, the purified spirits) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  ascend to the heavenly realms.") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 10 Tf
(Procedural Sequence / Observance Steps:) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  1. Identification of all community members who departed life during the) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  preceding twelve months.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  2. Crafting of wooden effigies or memorial seats for each departed soul.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  3. Lighting of resinous pine torches \(Mairong\) along village) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  thoroughfares at dusk.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  4. Antiphonal singing of Thisham Laa \(mourning laments\) by relatives and) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  village choirs.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  5. Ceremonial send-off offering food, rice beer, and travel provisions) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  for the soul's journey.) Tj
